<title>RUSSIA: Japan, Russia resume talks on $500 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Japan, Russia resume talks on $500 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government and Export-Import Bank of Japan have resumed talks on a $500 million credit to fund hospital equipment and baby food exports, a bank official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Kazuyuki Arasawa, one of the bank's representatives in Moscow, told Reuters that about $140 million would to go to carmaker AZLK Moskvich in Moscow, about $65 million will go to the city of Yuzhno-Sakhalinsk in the Far East and $61 million to the autonomous republic of Sakha to buy hospital equipment.</p>
<p>He said the talks, which started in 1994, were suspended following changes in the intergovernmental commission, which dealt with the talks.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
